summer 2017 was chock-full of great  films from blockbuster superhero sagas  to streaming only surprises franchises  were revived with bigger franchises were  brilliantly wrapped up legacies were  secured and Charlize Theron's probably  had more fun than anyone in the business  these are the best of the best from a  season full of fantastic films Wonder  Woman  after 75 odd years of whooping bad guy  but in the comic pages Wonder Woman  finally got her shot at solo blockbuster  glory just in time to either make or  break the emerging DC extended universe  Wonder Woman did everything it needed to  and then some serving as an effective  origin story as well as a superhero  adventure that stood on its own as a  standalone experience while continuing  to lay the groundwork for the DCE use  big team-up in Justice League the  reviews have been almost universally  positive and audiences have turned out  in droves laying the groundwork for a  real battle for superhero supremacy at  the box office between Marvel and DC  atomic blonde this neon thriller takes  place in the final days of the Cold War  the Berlin Wall is about to go down but  that doesn't mean the cloak-and-dagger  business is over to the contrary a super  spy played by Charlize Theron is sent to  Germany to retrieve a stolen list that  contains the names of undercover spies  the list has fallen into the hands of  the Soviets and Charlize will have to  bash a few skulls in request to discover  that document but honestly the plot  isn't that important the insane fight  choreography is the star here Charlize  beats up dudes using everything from  shoes to ropes to cooking pots all while  wearing the most stylish clothes  imaginable the actress did her own  stunts for atomic blonde adding a touch  of realism to the brutal battle scenes  and car chases  [Music]  okhta Netflix's okiya is a film that  starts off feeling like a g-rated kid's  adventure and ends up inside a very  r-rated slaughterhouse the film tells  the story of a young girl who's friends  with a hippo like super pig named okhta  that actually belongs to the  all-powerful mirando corporation a  business run by evil twins both played  by Tilda Swinton obviously okiya is  their genetically modified creation and  they plan on turning the poor pig into  the tastiest most eco-friendly pork  chops on the planet but not if the girl  in the team of animal activists rescue  okhta first a darkly comic vision of the  future okhta has quite a lot to say  about the evils of capitalism and the  merits of a plant-based diet while also  offering up a wildly entertaining and  inventive piece of filmmaking war for  the Planet of the Apes the conclusion to  one of the best film trilogies ever war  for the Planet of the Apes expertly  blends the book of Exodus with  Apocalypse Now resulting in a brutal Old  Testament pows story in the fiery  aftermath of the previous film Caesar  has led his followers into the mountains  hoping to escape the wrath of man but  Caesar knows his apes can't hide in the  hills for long so this primate Moses  plans on leading his people to a new  promised land where they can avoid any  future conflicts this sets up a bridge  on the river kwai style showdown between  Caesar and a mad colonel played by Woody  Harrelson war for the Planet of the Apes  is the perfect ending of the trilogy  featuring a show-stopping oscar-worthy  motion capture performance from Andy  Serkis spider-man homecoming one of the  most charming and entertaining films to  ever swing its way into the Marvel  Cinematic Universe  spider-man homecoming follows wannabe  Avenger Peter Parker as he tries to  fight crime and navigate high school at  the same time things get even more  complicated when an honest-to-goodness  supervillain shows up Michael Keaton's  vulture is the ultimate thief and a  feeder can bring him to justice it could  be his ticket into the Avengers one of  the best comic book movies ever made  homecoming even one over Marvel haters  thanks to its John Hughes like high  school vibe and all that upbeat energy  was largely thanks to Tom Holland who's  a pitch-perfect Peter Parker dunkirk  without a doubt the epic World War two  thriller Dunkirk is one of Christopher  Nolan's  latest achievements right up there with  inception in the dark night shot mostly  with 65 millimeter film on IMAX cameras  the nail-biting Dunkirk tells the story  of a real-life military retreat in 1940  roughly 400,000 Allied troops were  trapped on a French beach completely  surrounded and the only thing keeping  them from home was the English Channel  unfortunately the beach was too shallow  to accommodate military sized vessels so  English civilians sprang into action  sailing to Dunkirk in their yachts and  fishing boats  Nolan masterfully uses three  interlocking tails to put audiences  right in the middle of the battlefield  baby driver with its eclectic soundtrack  and insanely impressive driving stunts  Edgar Wright's baby driver is one of the  most exciting films of 2017 this  souped-up action flick starts ansel  elgort is baby a young man who works as  a getaway driver for a smarmy crime boss  played by Kevin Spacey suffering from  tinnitus baby drowns out the constant  droning with an incredible collection of  tunes to soundtrack his incredible  driving skills baby wants to go straight  but he gets pulled into a robbery gone  wrong so he's forced to take a stand to  save everything he loves with its dance  like action and it's super cool  characters write 6 feature film is like  a mash-up between singing in the rain  and Walter Hills the driver which means  it's got a little something for everyone  I want us to head west I never stop  anyway I mean baby thanks for watching  click the looper icon to subscribe to  our YouTube channel plus check out all  this cool stuff we know you'll love too  you
 

